{"id": "EUVD-2026-81581", "enisaUuid": "3488dba6-7f60-39a0-bf18-a426965ff53a", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.19 in prefill/decode disaggregation mode contains an unauthenticated PUT /route endpoint on the prefill bootstrap service that allows attackers to poison the KV transfer routing table. Attackers can supply arbitrary rank_ip and rank_port values to redirect decode workers to attacker-controlled endpoints, causing denial of service or disclosure of KV transfer metadata including session identifiers and tensor-parallel topology parameters.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T13:43:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-18T16:23:32", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/39400", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.19/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/common/conn.py#L1736-L1810", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.19/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/common/conn.py#L1716-L1718", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.19-unauthenticated-route-poisoning-via-put-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9hr3-qqwc-fxxh", "CVE-2026-92972"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f1ac5751-05f2-3c5b-b2d6-12b9f8683314", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.19"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a9212d56-2c51-3bb7-b833-48cada4cdb69", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}